# The self-improvement loop of d40, d42 and d44: a correction is filed as a lesson by
# whoever made it, the improver reads lessons rather than free text, and every lesson
# leaves the pile by a commit or by an answered rejection, never by deletion.
lesson file "the Lead dispatched a lane for a one-line doc fix" --expected "a one-line diff is done in place, with a card only for the claim" --why "a contract longer than the diff costs more than it protects" --target "recipe slp, Lane procedure" --evidence w41 --evidence h7
lesson file "the report named a candidate that was never verified" --expected "a done report names the sha the falsifier actually ran against" --why "an unverified candidate makes the gate a formality" --target "lead.md, reporting rule" --evidence w44
lesson list
lesson show l1
lesson process l1 --commit 1a2b3c4d
lesson process l2 --answer "the rule already says it; the lane misread it, so this is a prompt fix, not a doctrine edit"
lesson list
lesson list --all
